{"title":"View of Azalea Garden from Mt. Fuji, Hasui Kawase","link":"https://kottke.org/25/05/view-of-azalea-garden-from-mt-fuji-hasui-kawase","date":1748373522000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-08.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-08.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-08.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1946\" alt=\"woodblock print of a snow covered mountain with a field of flowers in the foreground\" /></p>\n\n<p>I love this gorgeous woodblock print from Hasui Kawase, View of Azalea Garden from Mt. Fuji. Hasui was <a href=\"https://faroutmagazine.co.uk/hasui-kawase-artist-inspired-studio-ghibli/\">a significant influence</a> on Studio Ghibli &amp; Hayao Miyazaki.</p>\n\n<blockquote><p>After all, the influence of Kawase on Ghibli, Miyazaki and his team of genius illustrators and animators is plain to see, and Miyazaki himself has previously stated his deep admiration for the legendary painter. The ability of Kawase to capture natural beauty alongside the human experience plays a significant part in Miyazaki’s love for Kawase, and it finds its way into several of the best Studio Ghibli films.</p>\n\n<p>The likes of My Neighbour Totoro, Spirited Away and Princess Mononoke all feature landscapes that are highly reminiscent of Kawase’s woodblock print style. Whether in the lush forests or beautiful countryside settings, it’s clear that Miyazaki was always keen on paying his respects to one of his favourite artists.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>Here are a few more of Hasui’s hundreds of works:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1950\" alt=\"woodblock print of a man walking in a forest of tall trees\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-03.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-03.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-03.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1878\" alt=\"woodblock print of a woman walking in the snow carrying an umbrella\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-04.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-04.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-04.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1183\" height=\"1600\" alt=\"woodblock print of green fields with mountains in the background\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-05.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-05.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-05.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"857\" alt=\"woodblock print of a horse-drawn wagon in front of bundles of bamboo\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-06.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-06.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-06.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1894\" alt=\"woodblock print of a sailboat on a lake\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-07.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-07.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hasui-kawase-07.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"1886\" alt=\"woodblock print of a winter scene\" /></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://mokuhanga1.com/kawase-hasui/\">You can find a large catalog of Hasui’s work here</a>, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Kawase_Hasui\">at Wikimedia Commons</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/7474079@N02/albums/72157676402408884/\">at Flickr</a>.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Hasui%20Kawase\">Hasui Kawase</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Hayao%20Miyazaki\">Hayao Miyazaki</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Japan\">Japan</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Studio%20Ghibli\">Studio Ghibli</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/05/view-of-azalea-garden-from-mt-fuji-hasui-kawase\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"1fcba5d62d164149466762877db04fc9c6cf2fee15d4eea85cb39cb02f88ff8b","category":"Sites"}